A||N||10||1986 Fiero||Can you help me?||||1||
Z||000000||1986 Fiero||03-20-2001||11:14 PM||||I just bought a 86 2m4 2.5L.The dog bone top motor mount is bad i have searched everywhere for one and no luck.I did call the Pontiac dealer and they have one for 45.00.Does anyone know where i can buy one cheaper or should i just pay this higher price....<P>Second question......I was driving my 2m4 today for the first time and i am only getting between 20-30 pounds of oil pressure while driving it.Do i need a new oil pump,or what should i do?<P>Does anyone know where i can buy fiero parts online? Can someone give me some web addresses....<P>            Thanks Alot ||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||03-20-2001||11:29 PM||||$45 sounds reasonable.....buy it.  The dogbone (especially on the 4-cyl.) is very important.  If you let it get really bad it will affect the motor mount and tranny mount....both of which are much harder to change than the dogbone.<P>As for your oil pressure problem.....you may just need a new sending unit.  Use a separate pressure gauge and check the pressure that way to determine what's really going on.  Sometimes the gauge itself reads incorrectly.  What does it read at idle?  <P>What type of parts are you looking for?  There are several people on this forum who sell parts (myself included).  Just post what you need in the mall section.  <P>For new stuff you may try the Fiero Store ( <A HREF="http://www.fierostore.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fierostore.com</A>  ).||||reg||1
Z||000002||tgowens||03-21-2001||01:39 AM||||go to the bottom of this page and look for the link for "Fiero Parts Vendors" there are many there who can be of help to you......||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jay||03-21-2001||09:26 AM||||I think $45 sounds steep!  I would look for a urethane bushing, stronger and come in different colors.  Try Race-Tech in Toronto, they ship to the US and you'd be paying in Canadian dollars (almost 1/2).  Number is 416-747-5728.<BR>I'f I remember correctly I think I paid about $50 Canadian for the V6 dog bone when I had a V6 in my car.||||reg||1
Z||000004||deceler8||03-21-2001||10:47 AM||||You should be able to get one from NAPA (an OE rubber bushing one) for $30 or so...I did about a year or so ago. If you don't have a NAPA in your town (doesn't every town have a NAPA ?), try their website.<P>Or get one off a junker (pre '86) and get a set of poly bushings (about $20) from Suspension Technologies.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/deceler8_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||862M4inCA||03-21-2001||11:02 AM||||If you have an Autozone nearby then you can get one there also, or most carquest autoparts stores carry them. I couldn't imagine it running more than about $40.||||reg||1
Z||000006||sqoach||03-21-2001||01:30 PM||||$45 for a dogbone engine mount!?!? i must have been lucky or something. i got one at my local o'reillys for $20. you could get one of those "super" dogbone's with the poly urethene bushings from the fierostore for about $45 i think. it just helps eliminate engine movement more than an OEM replacement with rubber bushings.<P>and for your oil pressure being low, i know this sounds obvious, but maybe you're low on oil.<P>and there are many online websites that sell stuff for us fiero guys. the fierostore only sells stuff for fieros. hence the name. and if you need something, just ask. i'm sure someone might have what you need.<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.JPG">  <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily driver)||||reg||1
Z||000007||1FST2M6||03-21-2001||01:44 PM||||or just call 1-800-LET-NAPA! and let Napa help you! <P>sorry.. that tape is in my car... I'd go with the Fiero Store Ultimate dog bone.. it cost a bit more but will outlast the car! ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Pontiaddict||03-24-2001||12:54 AM||||NAPA couldn't help me. They couldn't find the part in their books so I had to get one for another car that was like an inch longer ($10) until the Fiero Store sent me my ulitmate dogebone. Maybe you'll luck out though.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Chance||03-24-2001||11:09 PM||||The metal part of my Dog Bone was fine, but the rubber in it was bad.  I went to <A HREF="http://www.suspension.com/fiero-prothane.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.suspension.com/fiero-prothane.htm</A> <P>and got a polyurethane replacement bushings for it for 20 bucks americanUSD!<p>[This message has been edited by Chance (edited 03-24-2001).]||||reg||4
